---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---
<Marketing title="Install Goshikq from source" description="Clone the Goshikq repository, build the Rust runtime, and install unpublished Python and TypeScript SDKs from source." path="/download/">
  <section class="hero wrap prose">
    <p class="kicker">Install</p>
    <h1>Install from source</h1>
    <p class="lede"><strong>Packaged releases are not yet published.</strong> There is no PyPI, npm, or crates.io package and no GitHub Release archive. Use git or a development snapshot ZIP of <code>main</code>.</p>
    <h2>Source</h2>
    <pre class="install"><code>git clone {SITE.githubGit}</code></pre>
    <p><a href={SITE.github}>Open the repository</a></p>
    <h2>Development snapshot ZIP</h2>
    <p>This is the <code>main</code> branch, not an immutable release tag.</p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-secondary" href={SITE.zipMain}>Download main.zip</a></p>
    <h2>Python</h2>
    <p>Package name <code>{SITE.pythonPackage}</code> version <code>{SITE.pythonVersion}</code> is built locally. It is not on PyPI.</p>
    <pre class="install"><code>python -m pip install -e sdk/python
# extras (experimental providers): pip install -e "sdk/python[openai]" </code></pre>
    <h2>TypeScript / Bun</h2>
    <p><code>{SITE.tsPackage}@{SITE.tsVersion}</code> is not on npm. From the repo root:</p>
    <pre class="install"><code>bun install
bun --filter @goshikq/sdk test</code></pre>
    <h2>Rust runtime</h2>
    <pre class="install"><code>cargo run -p goshikq-server
# or: cargo build -p goshikq-server</code></pre>
    <h2>Docker</h2>
    <p>Compose file: <code>docker-compose.yml</code>. Postgres, runtime, and Studio images exist in tree. Production must not use <code>GOSHIKQ_AUTH_MODE=none</code>. A published image registry is not claimed.</p>
    <pre class="install"><code>docker compose up -d postgres</code></pre>
    <p>Without Docker: <code>DATABASE_URL=embedded</code>.</p>
    <h2>GitHub Releases</h2>
    <p>Packaged releases are not yet published. Install from source.</p>
  </section>
</Marketing>
